# The client randomness fields (d.cseed, d.cmath, d.cstat, d.cw) that
# test_snapshots does not compare yet for a recording, each with its cause.
# Every recording not named here is compared on all four. A line is
# RECORDING FIELD[,FIELD...]; lane/clientgate made this list, and it should
# only shrink: remove a line when its cause is fixed.

# A client mob copy's death: S19 status 3, then onDeathUpdate's 20 explode FX
# at particles 0. The native client keeps no health or death time for its
# copies of other entities.
cg-combat-pig-s1 d.cseed,d.cmath
combat-mobs-s1 d.cseed,d.cmath

# A client entity copy the native tracker never spawns (an S0F, an S11): the
# mobs of an unloaded or foreign dimension's chunks, peaceful's ghast, a
# dead player's orb.
end-unload-kinds-s1 d.cseed,d.cw
nether-unload-kinds-s1 d.cseed,d.cw
peaceful-s1 d.cseed,d.cmath
portal-foreign-s1 d.cseed,d.cmath
plate-dead-s1 d.cseed,d.cmath


# The client's Explosion.doExplosionB(true) over the S27's block list: the
# particle places and the ores' and spawner's drop draws are native's now
# (the S27 carries those blocks; struct-tnt-s42 compares), these two still
# draw differently on WorldClient.rand after a blast (a ghast's and a bed's,
# both flaming): not found yet.
cb-blockghast-s1 d.cw
end-bed-s42 d.cw

# A client-only fire: the oracle's WorldClient keeps a fire cell the server
# has cleared (doVoidFogParticles reads it), the native client world has
# the server's air.
endbot-s1 d.cw
endbot-s42 d.cw
gold-g30-s42 d.cw

# The client's chunk set after a reload or a dimension change: the oracle's
# WorldClient lacks a chunk (or a spawner's S35 entity) the native client
# has at that tick.
end-bed-exit-s1 d.cw
liq-reload-s1 d.cw,d.cseed,d.cmath
pearl-dims-s1 d.cw
sh-bot-west-s42 d.cw
sh-portal-s42 d.cw
tiles-reload-s1 d.cw
village-away-s42 d.cw,d.cseed,d.cmath

# The void fog's thousand samples read other client blocks than the
# oracle's (a few air cells more or fewer); the differing cells are not
# isolated yet.
end-return-s42 d.cw
end-throw-s42 d.cw
gold-g29-s42 d.cw
sh-bot-s42 d.cw
struct-dungeon-s42 d.cw
# (lane/longrun) Rows 5721 to 5745 only, after the teleport to x 5961,
# y 2, beside a lava lake whose still lava turns flowing: the oracle's
# snapshot at 5722 has one client chunk whose ids differ from its server's
# (clientworld.nbt differIds 1), native's client matches its server, and
# the void fog reads the other block. Every server field matches on all
# 30,100 rows.
explore-long-s1 d.cw

# A client mob copy walking on redstone ore (onEntityWalking's
# func_150186_m on WorldClient.rand): native's copies do not trigger
# walking.
gold-g5-s42 d.cw

# EffectRenderer.addBlockHitEffects: one FX the native dig flow does not
# make (gold-g17), one it makes the tick after the break, on the broken cell
# (break-place; its d.cw follows from that break).
gold-g17-s42 d.cseed,d.cmath
break-place-s1 d.cseed,d.cmath,d.cw

# The client's playAuxSFX 2002 (a thrown potion's splash): its draw count
# differs from the oracle's.
throw-items-s1 d.cw

# NetworkManager.processReceivedPackets handles at most 1001 packets a client
# tick and leaves the rest queued: a burst of spawns (334 orbs, mobs or items
# a tick in the oracle) reaches the client world over several ticks, each
# copy's constructor draws with it. Native's client world takes a tick's
# whole queue and does not count the packets it does not model.
crowd-600-s42 d.cseed,d.cmath
orb-heap-s1 d.cseed,d.cmath
tnt-cannon-s1 d.cseed,d.cmath
